{"id": "EUVD-2026-108754", "enisaUuid": "e8484149-509d-3783-a8cc-675f5d2215fc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: don't stash io_uring encoded data across -EAGAIN\n\nReturning -EAGAIN while leaving btrfs_uring_encoded_data in the cmd PDU\nleaks if the request is cancelled or the ring exits before reissue.\nio_uring does not free driver PDU allocations on cleanup.\n\nWrite: io_queue_sqe() always issues with IO_URING_F_NONBLOCK first, so\nreturn -EAGAIN before allocating and free data on every exit.\n\nRead: free on nowait -EAGAIN too; only -EIOCBQUEUED keeps the allocation\nfor btrfs_uring_read_finished().", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d9c1e0a7fb2cfb1cc924acafc194d2c15c3e83e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51562a8cb11628d3a5e105b4c347ec5473e5745f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98960"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3077ab50-7234-360a-bd53-84ff0b353902", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "4c70b4c2-c566-307f-be10-2f30d53b3d83", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34310c442e175f286b4c06ab5caa4e0b267ea31c <4d9c1e0a7fb2cfb1cc924acafc194d2c15c3e83e"}, {"id": "5b3afa65-fbb8-301c-96de-f878888e0ebc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "5e676ab7-e5a7-3607-90cc-629d0270fb65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34310c442e175f286b4c06ab5caa4e0b267ea31c <51562a8cb11628d3a5e105b4c347ec5473e5745f"}, {"id": "abeadc6d-bb25-3aaf-9989-cd2a28aad00c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d0999c5b-51dd-3577-9f53-84044e2d1c6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}